Core Emotion	Definition 	Synonyms	Antonyms	Masked Forms	Common Expressions	Need_State	Negative Cognitive Driver	Positive Cognitive Drivers	Intensity - Low	Intensity - Medium	Intensity - High	Ambiguity Triggers
Acceptance	Embracing reality or a situation as it is, without resistance, even when it feels uncomfortable.	Acknowledgment, tolerance, allowance	Rejection, denial, resistance	Passivity, emotional shutdown, over-rationalizing	The service wasn't quite what I expected, but I've accepted it for what it is.	Fairness	Fear of loss of control	Trust in process, self-compassion	Recognition	Adaptation	Surrender	
Admiration	A warm feeling of respect and appreciation for someone's qualities, actions, or character.	Respect, awe, reverence	Envy, disdain, disregard	Idealization, imitation, silent comparison	I genuinely admire how the staff handled our concerns. Truly impressive.	Recognition	Comparison-induced inadequacy	Motivation, value alignment	Respect	Appreciation	Reverence or idolization	
Affection	A gentle feeling of liking, care, or fondness toward someone or something.	Fondness, warmth, tenderness	Coldness, indifference, detachment	Friendliness without depth, obligation	The team made us feel genuinely cared for throughout our entire stay.	Belonging	Fear of being alone or unloved	Love, social bonding	Liking	Warmth	Deep emotional attachment	
Agitation	A restless inner discomfort often triggered by stress, frustration, or anticipation.	Restlessness, irritation, unease	Calmness, peace, contentment	Snappiness, pacing, forced productivity	The constant noise and lack of response made everything feel unsettled.	Safety	Overstimulation or frustration	Readiness for action, urgency to solve	Nervous energy	Irritation or tension	Visible restlessness or emotional dysregulation	
Agony	An overwhelming state of emotional or physical pain that feels hard to endure.	Torment, anguish, suffering	Comfort, ease, relief	Silence, numbing, withdrawal	This is unbearable. It hurts so much.	Safety	Powerlessness, emotional collapse	Call for help, emotional release	Deep hurt	Distress or despair	Desperation, sobbing, total breakdown	
Alarm	A sudden surge of fear or urgency in response to a perceived threat or danger.	Panic, alertness, fear	Composure, safety, trust	Overreacting, freezing, hypervigilance	When the fire alarm went off at 2am with no staff response, I panicked.	Safety	Hypervigilance	Quick response, risk assessment	Worry or unease	Alertness or racing heart	Panic or flight impulse	
Amazement	A feeling of wonder and surprise caused by something unexpected or extraordinary.	Wonder, awe, astonishment	Indifference, familiarity, apathy	Speechlessness, smiling disbelief	I couldn't believe how beautiful the property was. Absolutely stunning.	Recognition	Disbelief, emotional overload	Perspective shift, gratitude, inspiration	Surprise	Captivated attention	Total awe or shock	
Ambiguity	A sense of uncertainty or confusion due to unclear signals, meanings, or outcomes.	Uncertainty, vagueness, contradiction	Clarity, certainty, decisiveness	Indecision, sarcasm, avoidance	I wasn't sure if the issue had been resolved. No one followed up.	Competence	Cognitive dissonance	Tolerance for complexity, open-mindedness	Unclear feeling	Mixed emotions	Total inner conflict or emotional paralysis	
Ambivalence	Experiencing two conflicting emotions at the same time toward the same situation or person.	Inner conflict, mixed feelings, emotional duality	Certainty, commitment, resolve	Delay, overthinking, rationalizing	I loved the location but the service left me conflicted about returning.	Fairness	Insecurity or fear of consequences	Emotional intelligence, perspective holding	Minor indecision	Emotional tension	Paralysis or guilt over inaction	
Amusement	A light emotional response to something entertaining or mildly absurd.	Playfulness, delight, entertainment	Boredom, irritation, offense	Sarcasm, mockery, deflection	The concierge was genuinely funny and made our evening memorable.	Safety	Deflection or emotional masking	Joy, connection, perspective shift	Smirk or grin	Chuckle or smile burst	Laughter or inability to hold composure	
Anger	A strong emotional reaction to perceived injustice, threat, or boundary violation.	Rage, fury, frustration	Calm, forgiveness, acceptance	Sarcasm, silence, passive aggression	I've never been treated this poorly at any hotel. This was unacceptable.	Fairness	Injustice, powerlessness	Assertiveness, self-protection	Annoyance	Frustration or indignation	Rage or explosive reaction	
Anguish	Deep emotional pain often caused by loss, regret, or unresolved suffering.	Suffering, torment, despair	Relief, peace, joy	Withdrawal, numbness, distraction	After months of planning, the experience was devastating.	Belonging	Powerlessness, abandonment	Emotional honesty, vulnerability	Deep sorrow	Wounding or breakdown	Despair or existential pain	
Annoyance	A mild but persistent irritation triggered by repetitive or intrusive situations.	Irritation, bother, frustration	Contentment, calm, peace	Sarcasm, sighing, eye-rolling	Asked about the noise three times. Nothing was done.	Autonomy	Repetition or overstimulation	Attention to limits, push for change	Distraction or eye-rolling	Vocal irritation or complaint	Verbal snap or impulse to disengage	
Anticipation	A forward-looking emotional state centered on expecting a future event.	Expectation, hope, suspense	Indifference, apathy, surprise	Nervous excitement, overplanning	We had been looking forward to this trip for months.	Competence	Obsessive forecasting	Motivation, planning, hope	Mild curiosity	Eagerness or restlessness	Countdown mentality or tunnel vision	
Anxiety	A persistent feeling of worry, unease, or nervousness about something uncertain or uncontrollable.	Nervousness, dread, worry	Calmness, security, peace	Over-preparation, irritability, perfectionism	I kept worrying whether the reservation was properly set up.	Safety	Anticipated failure, lack of control	Vigilance, preparation	Butterflies or unease	Racing thoughts or restlessness	Panic attacks or avoidance	
Apathy	A state of emotional detachment marked by lack of interest, motivation, or response.	Indifference, disinterest, numbness	Passion, engagement, concern	Fatigue, blankness, disconnection	By the third day, staff seemed completely indifferent to our requests.	Safety	Emotional burnout or meaninglessness	Temporary psychological rest or retreat	Disengagement	Emotional flatness	Existential numbness or collapse	
Apprehension	A subtle form of fear centered on unease about what may go wrong in the near future.	Worry, dread, unease	Confidence, calm, trust	Overthinking, indecision, procrastination	Something felt off about the situation from the moment we checked in.	Competence	Fear of negative outcome	Risk assessment, caution	Gut check	Worry or tension	Avoidance or freezing	
Arousal	A heightened state of physiological and psychological alertness, which can be triggered by excitement, stress, or stimulation.	Stimulation, activation, alertness	Fatigue, calmness, numbness	Hyperactivity, impulsiveness, sexual tension	I‚Äôm on edge, I feel wired, My heart‚Äôs racing	Safety	Overstimulation or lack of control	Drive, readiness, excitement	Heightened attention	Restlessness or eagerness	Mania, impulsive action	
Awe	A deep emotional response to something vast, powerful, or profoundly moving that challenges your understanding or perspective.	Wonder, reverence, amazement	Dismissiveness, indifference, smallness	Silence, goosebumps, disorientation	I have never experienced anything so breathtaking in all my travels.	Competence	Insignificance	Transcendence, humility, curiosity	Subtle admiration	Emotional elevation or chills	Existential reverence or emotional overwhelm	
Awkwardness	A discomfort in social situations due to unclear roles, timing, or fear of being judged.	Embarrassment, discomfort, unease	Confidence, fluency, comfort	Nervous laughter, overcompensating, freezing	The interaction with the front desk was uncomfortable and confusing.	Belonging	Social insecurity	Self-awareness, humility	Momentary pause or silence	Blushing, rambling, avoidance	Wanting to disappear, panic in social setting	
Bafflement	A state of mental confusion where existing knowledge fails to explain what's being perceived.	Perplexity, puzzlement, bewilderment	Understanding, clarity, recognition	Laughing it off, freezing, double-checking	I still don't understand what happened with our reservation.	Belonging	Cognitive dissonance	Curiosity, reset, new framework	Minor confusion	Lost or mentally looping	Total disorientation or disbelief	
Befuddlement	A state of mental fogginess or confusion often caused by fatigue, overload, or emotional noise.	Fog, daze, disorientation	Alertness, clarity, focus	Zoning out, clumsiness, forgetfulness	After the third explanation, I was more confused than when I started.	Belonging	Overwhelm or cognitive fatigue	Signal for pause or recovery	Spaciness	Mental fog or disconnection	Temporary shutdown or disorientation	
Belonging	A deep feeling of acceptance and connection where one feels included and valued.	Connection, acceptance, inclusion	Isolation, exclusion, alienation	Over-adapting, people-pleasing	We felt like regulars from the very first moment we walked in.	Belonging	Fear of exclusion	Shared values, acceptance	Inclusion	Membership	Unity	
Bewilderment	Deep confusion following something unexpected or emotionally disorienting.	Dismay, bafflement, perplexity	Certainty, orientation, clarity	Silence, slow reactions	We had confirmed everything in advance. What happened was totally unexpected.	Competence	Loss of coherence	Reset of assumptions, new lens	Momentary pause	Lost or stunned	Emotional disarray or mental freeze	
Bitterness	A lingering emotional mix of anger and sadness rooted in unresolved hurt or resentment.	Resentment, grudge, cynicism	Forgiveness, peace, acceptance	Sarcasm, withdrawal, cold humor	After how they handled our complaint, I'll never forgive the experience.	Fairness	Betrayal or emotional scar	Boundary reinforcement, lesson from past	Quiet grudge	Persistent distrust	Chronic resentment	
Bittersweet	A mixed emotional state combining happiness with sadness or loss at the same time.	Mixed feelings, nostalgia, poignancy	Pure joy, indifference	Smiling through sadness, nostalgia	Our last night was magical, but leaving after everything that happened was hard.	Recognition	Loss of a moment or person	Gratitude for the experience	Poignancy	Melancholic joy	Overwhelming nostalgia	
Bliss	A deep sense of peace, joy, and contentment that feels complete and timeless.	Euphoria, serenity, ecstasy	Suffering, despair, turmoil	Stillness, smiling silence	Every detail was perfect. I didn't want it to end.	Belonging	Detachment from reality	Inner alignment, presence	Peaceful happiness	Joy or spiritual calm	Euphoric transcendence	
Boredom	A restless state caused by lack of stimulation, interest, or meaning.	Restlessness, monotony, dullness	Engagement, interest, excitement	Procrastination, distraction, scrolling	There was genuinely nothing to do in the evenings. No activities at all.	Competence	Stagnation or unmet cognitive needs	Catalyst for change or creativity	Mild restlessness	Disengagement or frustration	Existential dullness or agitation	
Brooding	A heavy, inward-focused emotional state marked by persistent, often negative rumination.	Rumination, gloom, preoccupation	Relief, openness, lightness	Silence, withdrawal, irritability	I keep replaying how they dismissed our concerns. Still bothers me.	Competence	Injustice or unprocessed pain	Meaning-making, introspection	Quiet reflection	Obsessive loops or self-blame	Emotional spiral or self-isolation	
Calmness	A stable emotional state where tension is low and the mind feels steady and at ease.	Peace, tranquility, composure	Anxiety, agitation, stress	Emotional suppression, avoidance	The atmosphere made it easy to fully relax and unwind.	Safety	Emotional shutdown or disengagement	Presence, emotional maturity	Ease	Stability or centeredness	Grounded equanimity	
Care	An emotional investment characterized by concern, responsibility, and attentiveness toward someone or something.	Concern, attentiveness, compassion	Neglect, indifference, apathy	Overhelping, control, self-sacrifice	You could tell the staff genuinely cared about getting every detail right.	Safety	Over-responsibility or fear of loss	Empathy, duty, loyalty	Soft attention	Nurturing involvement	Devotion or sacrifice	
Cheerfulness	A light, positive emotional state expressed through optimism, energy, and friendliness.	Brightness, positivity, good spirits	Gloom, sadness, irritability	Forced positivity, people-pleasing	The team's energy was infectious. Made the whole experience brighter.	Competence	Avoidance or masking	Optimism, playfulness	Smile or lightness	Laughing or teasing	Radiant, contagious energy	
Compassion	A deep awareness of another‚Äôs suffering paired with a desire to help or relieve it.	Empathy, kindness, understanding	Indifference, cruelty, detachment	Emotional distancing, over-giving	When they heard about our situation, they genuinely tried to help us.	Belonging	Compassion fatigue, self-neglect	Altruism, moral clarity	Warm attention	Emotional engagement	Deep urge to help or protect	
Confidence	A belief in one‚Äôs ability, judgment, or worth that supports action and self-expression.	Self-assurance, trust, certainty	Insecurity, doubt, fear	Defensiveness, arrogance	I knew immediately this team could deliver exactly what we needed.	Competence	Overcompensation or fear of appearing weak	Self-efficacy, preparation, clarity	Quiet self-belief	Assertiveness	Decisive presence or bold initiation	
Confusion	A mental and emotional state where meaning or direction feels unclear.	Disorientation, puzzlement, uncertainty	Clarity, understanding, certainty	Joking, avoidance, silence	Nobody could give us a straight answer about the check-in time.	Competence	Overload or lack of direction	Learning opportunity, humility	Momentary pause	Rereading or seeking clarity	Frozen or mentally overwhelmed	
Contempt	A feeling of superiority that dismisses or devalues another person or situation.	Disdain, scorn, disrespect	Respect, regard, appreciation	Sarcasm, eye-rolling, withdrawal	The attitude of the manager was dismissive and frankly disrespectful.	Autonomy	Superiority, moral rigidity	Value protection, discernment	Dismissiveness	Verbal jabs, eye-rolling	Social exclusion or humiliation	
Contentment	A quiet sense of satisfaction with what is present, without strong desire for change.	Satisfaction, ease, peace	Restlessness, dissatisfaction, longing	Complacency, disengagement	Everything was just right. I didn't need anything else.	Safety	Complacency, detachment	Appreciation, balance	Quiet pleasure	Sense of ease	Wholeness or spiritual stillness	
Courage	The emotional strength to act despite fear, risk, or uncertainty.	Bravery, resolve, fortitude	Fearfulness, avoidance, hesitation	Overcompensation, recklessness	I pushed myself to raise the issue directly with the manager.	Autonomy	Fear of regret or failure	Purpose, belief, resilience	Small act of risk	Choosing truth over comfort	Heroic or transformational action	
Curiosity	An emotional drive to explore, learn, or understand something new or unknown.	Interest, inquisitiveness, wonder	Apathy, disinterest, indifference	Restlessness, probing questions, distraction	I was curious how they'd handle such an unusual request.	Competence	Obsession or lack of focus	Exploration, growth mindset	Passing interest	Active questioning	Obsession with discovery	
Cynicism	A guarded emotional stance marked by distrust and negative assumptions about motives or outcomes.	Skepticism, mistrust, pessimism	Hope, trust, openness	Sarcasm, detachment, humor as defense	Another 'luxury' hotel that doesn't live up to the marketing.	Safety	Betrayal, repeated disappointment	Protection, critical thinking	Light sarcasm	General distrust	Complete skepticism or bitterness	
Defiance	An emotional resistance against control, pressure, or authority, driven by a need for autonomy.	Resistance, rebellion, opposition	Compliance, submission, surrender	Stubbornness, provocation, silence	I refused to just accept a non-solution and insisted on speaking to someone senior.	Autonomy	Perceived oppression or control	Self-assertion, boundary setting	Stubbornness	Resistance	Rebellion	
Dejection	A low emotional state marked by discouragement and loss of hope or motivation.	Discouragement, sadness, heaviness	Encouragement, optimism, uplift	Withdrawal, quiet resignation	After so many issues, we just felt beaten down and gave up asking.	Safety	Failure or unmet expectations	Rest, recovery, reevaluation	Mild discouragement	Hopelessness or gloom	Emotional collapse	
Delight	A strong feeling of pleasure and happiness sparked by something enjoyable or pleasing.	Joy, pleasure, enjoyment	Displeasure, dissatisfaction, misery	Contained excitement, smiling restraint	The breakfast spread was absolutely delightful. Exceeded every expectation.	Recognition	Overexcitement or dependence on external rewards	Gratitude, bonding, appreciation	Pleasant smile	Laughter or exclamation	Radiant joy or contagious excitement	
Despair	A profound sense of hopelessness where positive outcomes feel impossible.	Hopelessness, anguish, desolation	Hope, relief, optimism	Emotional shutdown, numbness	There was nothing left to salvage from the experience at that point.	Safety	Powerlessness, defeat	Vulnerability, call for help	Quiet hopelessness	Visible anguish	Existential collapse or suicidal ideation	
Disappointment	A feeling of letdown when expectations or hopes are not met.	Letdown, dissatisfaction, regret	Satisfaction, fulfillment, contentment	Suppressed frustration, polite acceptance	We expected so much more based on the reviews and the price we paid.	Fairness	Unmet expectations, idealism	Learning, resilience	Mild frustration	Emotional withdrawal	Disengagement or heartbreak	
Disgruntlement	A state of persistent dissatisfaction often mixed with irritation or resentment.	Dissatisfaction, annoyance, resentment	Contentment, satisfaction, ease	Complaining, passive resistance	Every small thing compounded until the frustration became impossible to contain.	Safety	Repeated neglect, invalidation	Desire for change, honesty	Grumbling or short tone	Venting or withdrawal	Outbursts or quitting	
Disgust	A strong emotional reaction of revulsion or rejection toward something offensive or unpleasant.	Revulsion, aversion, repulsion	Acceptance, attraction, tolerance	Avoidance, exaggerated reactions	The cleanliness standard was genuinely shocking.	Safety	Violation of personal or moral standards	Safety, instinct, discernment	Cringe or flinch	Verbal rejection	Physical reaction or rage	
Disillusionment	An emotional state arising when reality fails to match beliefs, ideals, or expectations.	Disenchantment, awakening, loss of illusion	Hope, idealism, belief	Emotional distancing, bitterness	I used to recommend this property. Not anymore.	Recognition	Betrayal, failed ideals	Wisdom, realism	Subtle distancing	Internal withdrawal	Existential doubt or collapse of worldview	
Dismissed	A feeling of being ignored, brushed off, or treated as unimportant, particularly when raising a concern or request.	Ignored, overlooked, brushed off, discounted, sidelined	Heard, acknowledged, valued, respected, attended to	Polite resignation, over-apologising for the request, withdrawing without complaint	They didn't even acknowledge us. It was as if we weren't there. I felt completely invisible.	Recognition	My concerns do not matter to this establishment	Being heard and acknowledged restores dignity	Slightly overlooked	Clearly ignored or brushed aside	Publicly dismissed or silenced	Polite but non-committal responses, lack of follow-through, vague reassurance
Displeasure	A mild to moderate feeling of dissatisfaction or irritation when something feels unpleasant or disappointing.	Dissatisfaction, irritation, annoyance	Pleasure, satisfaction, enjoyment	Polite restraint, subtle criticism	I'm not satisfied with how this was handled.	Safety	Lack of control or consideration	Self-protection, values assertion	Subtle tension	Critical feedback	Overt objection	
Distress	A state of emotional strain or suffering caused by overwhelming pressure, fear, or pain.	Anguish, anxiety, turmoil	Relief, calm, comfort	Emotional shutdown, overfunctioning	By the time we reached the third night, I was completely overwhelmed.	Safety	Loss of control, perceived danger	Urgency, alert for help	Inner restlessness	Visible anxiety or worry	Emotional collapse or panic attack	
Distrust	A lack of confidence in someone or something, driven by suspicion or past experience.	Suspicion, wariness, doubt	Trust, confidence, assurance	Guarded behavior, testing others	After what happened, I don't trust this property to deliver on any promise.	Safety	Past betrayal or manipulation	Self-protection, due diligence	Subtle hesitation	Vocal skepticism	Rejection or complete disengagement	
Dread	An intense fear or apprehension about something anticipated in the future.	Fear, terror, foreboding	Relief, safety, calm	Avoidance, procrastination	I was dreading having to go back to that front desk again.	Safety	Fear of pain, failure, or loss	Risk awareness, protective instincts	Nervous anticipation	Avoidance or paralysis	Severe anxiety or panic	
Eagerness	An excited readiness to engage with or experience something desired.	Enthusiasm, readiness, anticipation	Reluctance, apathy, hesitation	Overcommitment, impatience	We couldn't wait to try every amenity they had to offer.	Safety	Fear of missing out or being left behind	Optimism, motivation, anticipation	Mild enthusiasm	Assertive engagement	Impulsive action or impatience	
Ecstasy	An overwhelming feeling of intense joy or pleasure that feels all-consuming.	Euphoria, rapture, bliss	Misery, despair, suffering	Emotional overflow, impulsivity	The spa experience was absolutely transcendent. Nothing short of extraordinary.	Belonging	Addictive reward-seeking	Spiritual alignment, ultimate joy	Euphoric smile	Overwhelming joy	Out-of-body bliss or spiritual unity	
Embarrassment	A self-conscious emotional response to perceived social mistakes or unwanted attention.	Self-consciousness, shame, discomfort	Confidence, ease, composure	Nervous laughter, avoidance	It was mortifying to have our booking issue discussed loudly in the lobby.	Fairness	Fear of judgment, social rejection	Humility, self-awareness	Blushing or laughing it off	Avoidance or overexplaining	Social withdrawal or panic	
Empathy	The ability to emotionally understand and share the feelings of another person.	Understanding, compassion, resonance	Indifference, detachment, apathy	Over-identification, emotional fatigue	The staff understood exactly what kind of experience we needed.	Belonging	Emotional overload, blurred boundaries	Compassion, care, attunement	Recognition of others‚Äö√Ñ√¥ feelings	Emotional alignment	Absorbing others‚Äö√Ñ√¥ pain or joy	
Emptiness	A hollow emotional state marked by a lack of feeling, meaning, or connection.	Hollowness, numbness, void	Fulfillment, connection, meaning	Distraction, overconsumption	Despite everything being technically fine, it felt hollow and impersonal.	Belonging	Disconnection, unresolved grief	Self-reflection, emotional reset	Subtle disinterest	Lack of motivation or detachment	Existential despair or numbness	
Enchantment	A feeling of being captivated or charmed by something magical, beautiful, or inspiring.	Fascination, captivation, wonder	Disillusionment, boredom, indifference	Idealization, romanticizing	The setting was utterly magical. I was completely captivated.	Recognition	Escapism, illusion	Creativity, spiritual uplift	Momentary charm	Absorbed focus or joy	Transcendent awe or obsession	
